  "title": "UK Salmonella Outbreak: London and Yorkshire Among Regions Reporting the Most Cases",
  "summary": "A growing salmonella outbreak in the UK has prompted an investigation by public health authorities after more than 200 infections were recorded over the past year. Health officials are examining a possible connection with eggs imported from outside the UK, while warning the public about the symptoms of salmonella and ways to reduce the risk of infection. According to figures reported by the UK Health Security Agency (UKHSA), 207 cases were identified between 11 August 2025 and 1 August 2026. Mo",
